<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ContentView xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="Plutus.Frontend.AppClient.Pages.CustomViews.InputAlert">
    <!--
        ⚠ THE SCROLLVIEW IS NOT COSMETIC — WITHOUT IT THIS DIALOG SILENTLY LOSES FIELDS.

        `MainLayout` is capped at 90% of the window height in `OnSizeAllocated`, and a bare
        StackLayout does not scroll: anything past the cap is CLIPPED, invisible, with nothing to
        say so. The file already carried a warning that a cash grid plus entries plus three buttons
        clipped Confirm off the bottom — and then the item editor grew to eight rows and reproduced
        it. Matt, 2026-08-11: *"Edit item, I can ONLY change the tax? This doesn't seem right."*
        The other fields were there. They were below the fold.

        ⚠ A clipped dialog is worse than a broken one. A broken one gets reported; this one looks
        like a deliberately small feature, so the operator concludes the software cannot do it.

        ⚠ The height cap moves ONTO the ScrollView. Leaving it on the inner stack would cap the
        content and give the scroller nothing to scroll.
    -->
    <ContentView.Content>
        <ScrollView x:Name="Scroller"
                    HorizontalOptions="CenterAndExpand"
                    VerticalOptions="CenterAndExpand"
                    BackgroundColor="White">
            <StackLayout
                x:Name="MainLayout" Padding="10,10,10,10"
                Spacing="5" BackgroundColor="White"
                HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand"
                VerticalOptions="StartAndExpand"/>
        </ScrollView>
    </ContentView.Content>
</ContentView>
